# GrowthKit Client-Side Widget Integration Guide

## Installation

```bash
npm install @fenixblack/growthkit
# or
pnpm add @fenixblack/growthkit
```

## Environment Configuration

Set up your public API key in `.env.local`:
```
NEXT_PUBLIC_GROWTHKIT_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_your_public_key_here
```

> **Important**: Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_GROWTHKIT_PUBLIC_KEY` (not `API_KEY`) - this is the correct environment variable name.

## Basic Integration (KISS Approach)

Integrate directly in your main page component where you have access to language context:

```tsx
"use client"

import { useRef, useEffect } from "react"
import { GrowthKitAccountWidget, type GrowthKitAccountWidgetRef } from "@fenixblack/growthkit"
import { useLanguage } from "@/contexts/language-context"

export default function Page() {
  const { language } = useLanguage()
  const growthKitRef = useRef<GrowthKitAccountWidgetRef>(null)

  // Sync GrowthKit language when page language changes
  useEffect(() => {
    if (growthKitRef.current) {
      growthKitRef.current.setLanguage(language)
    }
  }, [language])

  return (
    <GrowthKitAccountWidget
      ref={growthKitRef}
      config={{
        publicKey: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_GROWTHKIT_PUBLIC_KEY || '',
        language: language,
        theme: 'auto' // 'light' | 'dark' | 'auto'
      }}
      position="bottom-right" // 'top-right' | 'top-left' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom-right'
      slim={true} // Use minimal display
    >
      {/* Your page content */}
    </GrowthKitAccountWidget>
  )
}
```

## Language Synchronization

The key to language sync is the `useEffect` that watches for language changes:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (growthKitRef.current) {
    growthKitRef.current.setLanguage(language)
  }
}, [language])
```

This automatically syncs the widget language whenever your page language changes via your language selector.

## Credit Consumption

Access the GrowthKit hook for credit management:

```tsx
import { useGrowthKit } from "@fenixblack/growthkit"

function MyComponent() {
  const gk = useGrowthKit()
  
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Credits: {gk.credits}</h1>
      
      <button 
        onClick={() => gk.completeAction('generate_content')}
        disabled={!gk.canPerformAction('generate_content')}
      >
        Generate Content (costs credits)
      </button>
      
      <button onClick={() => gk.share()}>
        Share & Earn Credits
      </button>
    </div>
  )
}
```

